 "speech": {
  "language": "en",
  "text": "If you're running medical practice here in the South Bay of the Greater Los Angeles area you're trying to grow a high value service, you might not actually need more leads. You just might need to stop losing the ones you're already paying for. Think about what happens when somebody actually out of form. How quickly does someone respond? What happens if they don't answer? Who follows up tomorrow? Five days later? Two weeks later? And how easy is it for that person to actually be on your calendar? Because generating a lead is only one part of the patient acquisition. Rose, we look at the entire journey, the advertising, the funnel, the response time, the follow -up, the appointment and setting process, and what happens after somebody raises their hand. Because spending more money on leads won't fit a broken conversion process. And this is exactly what we look back in a patient acquisition audit. We trace your whole entire acquisition from first inquiry, the response, follow -up, and booking to identify where the opportunities may be falling through. If your goal is to get more qualified appointments on the calendar, request a patient acquisition audit below, and let's go over together.",
